{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And you shall trade in the land</b> — they altered the matter to him for the sake of peace, so that he would agree to send Benjamin with them, for had they wished they could have immediately returned, had he not said, \"My son shall not go down with you.\" Similarly, they said to him, \"Your one brother you left with me,\" and they did not tell him about their imprisonment, nor about the imprisonment of Simeon. And it is possible that Joseph said to them, \"And you shall trade in the land,\" but Scripture did not record it, his intention being: bring merchandise as you wish to purchase the grain, and I will not take the value of your merchandise, for I will do good to you in exchange for your shame. And likewise, \"The man asked us particulars about us and about our kindred\" (Genesis 43:7) — this was an excuse to their father, or as they said to him, \"We are all sons of one man,\" he said to them: No, but in truth you have come to see the nakedness of the land, and tell me whether your father is still alive and whether you have another brother, for I will investigate you and know what you are. Then they answered: We are twelve brothers, sons of one man, and he is in the land of Canaan today, for he is still alive, and the youngest is with him and one is no more. And this is what Judah said (Genesis 44:19), \"My lord asked his servants, saying, Have you a father or a brother?\" And similarly in many places Scripture abbreviates in the narrative or in the account, as I have mentioned (above, Genesis 24:22, 31:7). And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 42:34), \"תִּסְחָרוּ\" — \"you shall go around,\" and every term of סְחוֹרָה and סוֹחֲרִים is so called because they go around (מְסַבְּבִים) after merchandise. It appears that the Rav wished to be precise here, that all he said was that they would be permitted to go around the land and purchase grain as they wished at all times, and he did not explain likewise (Genesis 34:10) \"dwell and trade in it,\" (v. 21) \"and they shall trade in it.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:23.894410931Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}